Peter Snelling (snelling@bnr.ca) wrote:
: Has everyone tried the #adjust feature in 3.1?  I use it all the time...
:    I keep a Key in letter "k"
:    I keep a Whistle in letter "w"
:    I keep food rations in letter "e" (eat e)
:    I keep holy water in letter "d" (#dip in d)
:    I often keep my main weapon in "a" (just because)

: I think it's great!

I also use it to organize my items when I go to identify so the things
that need to be identified are ordered in levels of importance.  For
example if the first ring in my ring list is already identified, I swap
it with a ring that isn't.  It makes identifying a large inventory much
easier.  It also makes sure I get the important stuff before the
unimportant stuff, like indentifing an unknown wand before indentifying
a known wand with unknown charges.

